Build test-crt-posixc-general, test-crt-posixc-vfork-fd-thread and
test-crt-posixc-close-pipe-progress.

Run fd_reservation, vfork_context, vfork_fd and vfork_fd_thread without arguments.
Each program returns zero on success. The descriptor matrix runs nofork,
vfork/_exit, inherited-byte, exec and CLOEXEC cases in one invocation. It locates
itself through PROGDIR and argv[0]. waitpid uses bounded WNOHANG polling and logs
errno immediately on failure. Byte and EOF checks run after child exit and after
the parent closes its remaining writer.

close_pipe_progress checks that closing a duplicate reader does not lock the
table behind blocking pipe IO. A delayed direct-DOS writer releases the reader
on the old lock implementation too.

These tests do not qualify concurrent entry into the shared pretend-child CRT
context, forced termination, process-tree cancellation or concurrent IO versus
close of the same descriptor.
